A grand concert hall interior in the style of Piet Mondrian, with the architecture broken into bold geometric sections of primary red, yellow, and blue separated by thick black lines. Multiple doorways of different shapes and sizes are scattered illogically across the walls, but all converge toward a single luminous central stage where a lone musician sits at a piano. Streams of colorful geometric shapes—rectangles, squares, and lines—flow from each doorway, merging and harmonizing as they approach the performer, transforming from chaotic fragmented paths into one unified composition of balanced blocks and colors surrounding the stage. The perspective is from the back of the hall looking forward, with abstract audience figures represented as simple geometric forms in complementary colors, all facing the same unified focal point.
